<h1 id="gptex-title" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0">ChatGPT share extraction (<code>gptex</code>)</h1>

**Trigger:** User types **`gptex`** and provides a **ChatGPT share** URL (or asks to extract from one). Scope is the **active project** (its **`utils/chatgpt/`** tree).

**Canonical how-to:** **`utils/chatgpt/HOWTO_EXTRACT_CHATGPT.md`** — JSON API, Playwright when needed, caveats, file layout.

**Code layout (this repo):**

- **`utils/chatgpt/playwright/`** — Node + Playwright (`package.json`, `fetch_share.mjs`, `extract_transcript.mjs`, **README**).
- Follow the HOWTO’s **install and run** steps; do not invent transcript text — use the documented fetch/extract path.

**Workflow:** Read the HOWTO → run or adapt the **playwright** scripts as documented → place outputs per the HOWTO (e.g. **`transcripts/`**, **`test_result/`** as applicable).

**Do not:** Scrape the share page HTML as if it were the full conversation; use the **backend API** and/or **Playwright** flow from the HOWTO.
